    <briefdescription>
<para>Android, chrono-compatible, suspend-aware clock. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Linux steady clock is represented by <computeroutput>CLOCK_MONOTONIC</computeroutput>. However, this implementation does not work properly for long-running clocks that work in the background when the system is suspended.</para>
<para><computeroutput><ref refid="structsf_1_1SuspendAwareClock" kindref="compound">SuspendAwareClock</ref></computeroutput> uses <computeroutput>CLOCK_BOOTTIME</computeroutput> which is identical to <computeroutput>CLOCK_MONOTONIC</computeroutput>, except that it also includes any time that the system is suspended.</para>
<para>Note: In most cases, <computeroutput>CLOCK_MONOTONIC</computeroutput> is a better choice. Make sure this implementation is required for your use case. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
